@startuml
' NewEra POS - System sequence diagram of UC5 Return Rental (main scenario and main variants), W09
' Team D - editable source of assets/ssd_uc5.png
' Render with: java -jar plantuml.jar -tpng assets/ssd_uc5.puml
' Step numbers refer to UC5 in docs/requirements/SRS.md (W09).

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 130
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #444444
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF1FB
skinparam ActorBorderColor #444444
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam SequenceGroupBackgroundColor #F4F8FD
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam SequenceDividerBackgroundColor #EAF1FB
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B8A04A
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title NewEra POS - System sequence diagram: UC5 Return Rental

actor ":Cashier" as Cashier
participant ":NewEra POS" as POS <<system>>

note over Cashier, POS
  Precondition: a cashier session is open (UC4) and the item was rented with UC3.
  The Customer takes part only through the Cashier. The Payment Service,
  the Tax Calculator and the Accounting System are inside the black box.
end note

== Start the rental return (UC5 steps 2-3) ==
Cashier -> POS : makeNewRentalReturn()
activate POS
POS --> Cashier : new rental return opened
deactivate POS

== Find the open rental (steps 4-5) ==
Cashier -> POS : findRental(code)
activate POS
alt open rental found
  POS --> Cashier : customer, item, rental date, due date, deposit and tender of the rental
else no open rental for this code (5a)
  POS --> Cashier : "No open rental for this item"
end
deactivate POS
note right of POS
  code = serial number of the item or rental receipt number.
  No receipt and no readable serial number (5b): the Cashier enters
  the customer ID with findRentalsOfCustomer(customerID) and
  selects the rental with selectRental(rentalID).
end note

== Check the item (steps 6-7) ==
Cashier -> POS : recordCondition(condition, damageNote)
activate POS
alt undamaged, on time
  POS --> Cashier : no late fee; refund = the full deposit
else undamaged, after the due date (7a)
  POS --> Cashier : days late, late fee, tax of the late fee;\nrefund = deposit - late fee - tax (never below zero)
else undamaged, late fee and tax larger than the deposit (7b)
  POS --> Cashier : days late, late fee, tax of the late fee;\nrefund = 0 and the amount still due (late fee + tax - deposit)
  Cashier -> POS : makePayment(amount, tenderType)
  activate POS
  POS --> Cashier : payment accepted, as in UC1 (9a-9c);\nthe Cashier then confirms the rental return
  deactivate POS
else damaged (6a)
  POS --> Cashier : a store manager must confirm the damage
  Cashier -> POS : confirmDamage(managerID, pin)
  activate POS
  POS --> Cashier : damage confirmed; refund = 0 (the whole deposit is kept)
  deactivate POS
end
deactivate POS
note right of POS
  The tax of the late fee comes from the Tax Calculator (default rate if it is not available,
  7a1). When the item is damaged and late, the late fee is only recorded (6a4).
  makePayment is sent only in 7b, before confirmRentalReturn; a failed payment
  (declined card, no answer) is handled as in UC1 (BR-18: the Cashier can use another tender).
end note

== Confirm and refund (steps 8-11) ==
Cashier -> POS : confirmRentalReturn()
activate POS
alt refund is zero (damaged item, or 7b already paid)
  POS --> Cashier : no refund is paid; rental return receipt
  deactivate POS
else rental paid in cash (9a)
  POS --> Cashier : refund due in cash (drawer opens), rental return receipt
  deactivate POS
else rental paid by credit card (9b)
  note right of POS
    The POS sends the refund request, with the reference of the rental
    payment, to the Payment Service.
  end note
  alt refund approved
    POS --> Cashier : card refund done, rental return receipt
    deactivate POS
  else declined (9b2a)
    POS --> Cashier : reason; no cash is paid, a store manager must approve a cash refund
    deactivate POS
    Cashier -> POS : approveCashRefund(managerID, pin, reason)
    activate POS
    POS --> Cashier : refund due in cash (drawer opens), rental return receipt
    deactivate POS
  else no answer (9b2b)
    POS --> Cashier : no cash is paid; the POS asks for the refund status\n(done, failed as 9b2a, or pending: a store manager completes it later)
    deactivate POS
  end
else rental paid by check (9c, Could)
  POS --> Cashier : a check cannot be refunded; a store manager must approve a cash refund
  deactivate POS
  Cashier -> POS : approveCashRefund(managerID, pin, reason)
  activate POS
  POS --> Cashier : refund due in cash (drawer opens), rental return receipt
  deactivate POS
end

note over Cashier, POS
  After the refund the POS saves the rental return, closes the rental, changes the item status
  (Available if undamaged, Under maintenance if damaged), queues the AccountingRecord
  and prints the rental return receipt (steps 10-11). Cancel before confirming: cancelRentalReturn() (8a).
end note
@enduml
